<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\SnapZap.Core\SnapZap.Core.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The optional sidecar, installed by scripts/install-deps.{sh,bat} into <repo>/models. The app
    resolves it relative to AppContext.BaseDirectory, so without this copy a freshly installed
    model would sit in the repo while the app looked for it in bin/Debug/net10.0/models and
    reported "Not installed".

    Never fails a build: the glob matches nothing when the model isn't installed, which is the
    supported state — SnapZap scans, dedups, exports and deletes without it.

    Excluded from publish on purpose. The published output is the shipping artifact, where
    including a 328 MB model is a deliberate choice rather than a side effect of having run
    the installer locally. To ship it, install into the publish directory directly by passing
    the installer's "dest" option, e.g. dest artifacts/win-x64.

    The companion glob over <repo>/tools was dropped in dedup v2: it existed to stage
    czkawka_cli, and similar-image detection is now in-process (docs/DEDUP-V2.md). Leaving it
    would keep copying a 47 MB binary nothing calls into every build output.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)..\..\models\*"
             Link="models\%(Filename)%(Extension)"
             CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest"
             CopyToPublishDirectory="Never"
             Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
